Description: Accept software decoded frames in vo=avfoundation by uploading
 them into a pooled CVPixelBuffer.
 .
 VideoToolbox has no hardware path for VP9, MPEG-2, VC-1 or MPEG-4 ASP, and
 none for AV1 before A17 Pro. A hardware only output shows nothing at all for a
 broadcast stream or an older file, and the server will not step in because the
 device profile claims those codecs are playable.
 .
 Only NV12 and P010 are accepted, so mpv converts anything else on the way in
 rather than this output growing its own conversion. Buffers come from a pool
 and are IOSurface backed, which the display layer requires. Uploads are tagged
 with the stream's colour, since unlike hardware frames they arrive as bytes
 with no such history.
Author: Plankton
Origin: other
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-08-10

